{"id":"n4-040","title":"Verb て くる","romaji":"Verb te kuru","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"An action that starts in the past and continues to the present or future; 'come to', 'begin to', 'become'.","longExplanation":"The て くる grammar point is used to express an action that starts in the past and continues to the present or future. It can also show a change in state or condition. The formation involves attaching the て-form of the verb followed by くる.","formation":"Verb て-form + くる","examples":[{"jp":"最近、日本語が分かってくるようになりました。","romaji":"Saikin, nihongo ga wakatte kuru you ni narimashita.","en":"Recently, I've come to understand Japanese.","words":[{"surface":"最近","vocabId":"1293780","reading":"さいきん"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日本語","vocabId":"1464530","reading":"にほんご"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"分かっ","vocabId":"1606560","reading":"わかる","baseForm":"分かる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"くる","vocabId":null},{"surface":"よう","vocabId":null},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"なり","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"なる"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[6]},{"jp":"寒くなってきたので、コートを着ましょう。","romaji":"Samuku natte kita node, kooto wo kimashou.","en":"Since it's gotten cold, let's put on a coat.","words":[{"surface":"寒く","vocabId":"1210360","reading":"さむく","baseForm":"寒い"},{"surface":"なっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"なる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"き","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"くる"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ので","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"コート","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"着ましょう","vocabId":"1423000","reading":"きましょう","baseForm":"着る"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[3]},{"jp":"雨がやんできました。","romaji":"Ame ga yande kimashita.","en":"The rain has stopped (and it's cleared up).","words":[{"surface":"雨","vocabId":"1171900","reading":"あめ"